 new species  called the cat and if you're curious  what her name is it's PB  on top of that bioware also confirmed  that loyalty missions from mass effect 2  will return and you will be able to get  it on with your crew members  as well as becoming the new Pathfinder  it sounds like you will also have access  to plenty of new weapons vehicles and  tools the new mako like all-terrain  vehicle is called the nomads and it will  be key when it comes to exploring  planets the normandy replacement is  called The Tempest it looks bigger than  the Normandy but we don't really know  much about it hopefully we will be able  to pilot this thing the leaks and rumors  say yes but we'll just have to wait for  an official word from bioware on that  one the Andromeda initiated video also  showed off some new and returning  weapons the carnufex is back as well as  the tempest from two and three it sounds  like you will also have the ability to  establish colonies on planets you  explore we don't know the specifics on  this one but I have a feeling it could  play a big role in Andromeda and finally  we haven't seen much of the gameplay but  according to Mac Walters creative  director Andromeda will attempt to  strike a balance between action and  role-playing there will be destructible  environments to 24 player multiplayer  and new biotics and other skills even  with all this new info there is still  plenty we don't know about Andromeda and  that just might be the most exciting  thing about it Andromeda is scheduled  for a spring 2017 release date but in  the meantime stay tuned to gamespot all  the time has come to prepare ourselves  for a future beyond the Milky Way a  future that begins 600 years from where  we stand in a time place among unknown  stars and unseen dangers  and so we issue this calls to the brave  the inquisitive to the Trailblazers of  the human race as an invitation to stand  on the shoulders of those who came  before and challenge yourself to go  further begin